-- Nested blocks (E7): the recursor's type is guarded (the motives)
-- --------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- --------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Nested blocks (E7): the recursor's type is guarded (a minor premise)
-- --------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- --------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Nested blocks (E7): the recursor's type is guarded (an inductive hypothesis's type, a minor premise)
-- --------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- --------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Nested blocks (E7): the recursor's type is guarded (the minors' telescope, the tail)
-- --------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- --------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Nested blocks (E7): the recursor's rule at every block
-- --------------------------------------------------------------------------

--| The recursor's rule in the model from the rule's premises (`ind_rec_ty`), at every block: the restored type has the value
--| of the type `rec_ty` builds, because that type is guarded under the parameters.
theorem ind_rec_ty_all (G: hyps) (H J: class) (u w r tg td tv ti tN tR0 tRT: set):
  $ G ⇒ iwf u H J tg td w r $ > $ G ⇒ hctor ⊆ H $ > $ G ⇒ hrec ⊆ H $ > $ G ⇒ ra_elim_ok tg td tv ∈ lrel3 J $ > $ G ⇒ ra_rec_ty td tv ti tR0 ∈ lrel $ > $ G ⇒ ra_ind_nested td tN ∈ lrel $ > $ G ⇒ ra_rst td tN tR0 tRT ∈ lrel $ > $ G ⇒ tR0 ∊ ofsort lsig lopen ks_expr $ > $ G ⇒ ti ∊ ofsort lsig lopen ks_nat $ >
  $ G ⇒ dt u (mcv H) ⟨ kc_ind_rec , scons td (scons ti (scons tv ∅)) ⟩ w r ∈ dt u (mcv H) tRT w r $;

-- --------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Nested blocks (E7): the type of a projection at every block
-- --------------------------------------------------------------------------

--| The type of a projection in the model from the rule's premises (`proj_ty`), at every block: the field's type is guarded
--| at the field's depth (`f147_np`), so its restored form has the same value over the earlier fields and the parameters.
theorem proj_ty_all (G: hyps) (H J: class) (u w r r0 tg td tb tp tt tnp ti tS tfi tN tA tA2 tA1 tR te te2: set):
  $ G ⇒ iwf u H J tg td w r0 $ >
  $ G ⇒ hctor ⊆ H $ >
  $ G ⇒ r ∊ sat u (mcv H) tg w $ >
  $ G ⇒ dt u (mcv H) te w r = dt u (mcv H) te2 w r $ >
  $ G ⇒ dt u (mcv H) te w r ∈ dt u (mcv H) tS w r $ >
  $ G ⇒ ra_spine ⟨ kc_ind_ty , scons td (scons ti ∅) ⟩ tS tnp ∈ lrel $ >
  $ G ⇒ ra_ind_data td tb tp tt ∈ lrel $ >
  $ G ⇒ ra_struct_like td ti ∈ lrel $ >
  $ G ⇒ ra_proj_ok tg td ti tfi ∈ lrel3 J $ >
  $ G ⇒ ra_clen tp tnp ∈ lrel $ >
  $ G ⇒ ra_field_ty td ti tfi tA ∈ lrel $ >
  $ G ⇒ ra_ind_nested td tN ∈ lrel $ >
  $ G ⇒ ra_rst td tN tA tA2 ∈ lrel $ >
  $ G ⇒ ra_pinst tfi tS tA2 tA1 ∈ lrel $ >
  $ G ⇒ ra_qinst tb te tfi ⟨ kc_nz , ∅ ⟩ tA1 tR ∈ lrel $ >
  $ G ⇒ te2 ∊ trees ω $ >
  $ G ⇒ tS ∊ ofsort lsig lopen ks_expr $ >
  $ G ⇒ dt u (mcv H) ⟨ kc_proj , scons tb (scons tfi (scons te ∅)) ⟩ w r = dt u (mcv H) ⟨ kc_proj , scons tb (scons tfi (scons te2 ∅)) ⟩ w r ∧ dt u (mcv H) ⟨ kc_proj , scons tb (scons tfi (scons te ∅)) ⟩ w r ∈ dt u (mcv H) tR w r $;

-- --------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Nested blocks (E7): restoring a telescope
-- --------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- --------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Nested blocks (E7): the computation rules at every block
-- --------------------------------------------------------------------------

--| `aeq` in the model, with every atom of `J` true: the two sides have one value at a valuation of the context (by induction
--| on the term: one head, or applications of `aeq` functions to arguments that `J` makes equal). No spine is needed.
theorem aeq_dt (G: hyps) (J M: class) (u w c r te tt: set):
  $ G ⇒ jval u M J $ >
  $ G ⇒ w ∊ lvals $ >
  $ G ⇒ r ∊ sat u M c w $ >
  $ G ⇒ ra_aeq c te tt ∈ lrel3 J $ >
  $ G ⇒ dt u M te w r = dt u M tt w r $;

--| The projection of a constructor application in the model from the rule's premises (`proj_mk`), at every block: the
--| constructor's type is restored inside `ctor_ty`, and the major premise's arguments are a valuation of the unrestored
--| context all the same (`f150_ca`: a restored telescope has the same valuations over the parameters).
theorem proj_mk_all (G: hyps) (H J: class) (u w r r0 tg td tnp tn tm ti tCT tnf tnq tmj tT2 tfi tii tY tf tb2: set):
  $ G ⇒ iwf u H J tg td w r0 $ >
  $ G ⇒ hctor ⊆ H $ >
  $ G ⇒ r ∊ sat u (mcv H) tg w $ >
  $ G ⇒ ra_spine ⟨ kc_ind_ctor , scons td (scons ti (scons ⟨ kc_nz , ∅ ⟩ ∅)) ⟩ tmj tnq ∈ lrel $ >
  $ G ⇒ ra_ind_arity td tnp tn tm ∈ lrel $ >
  $ G ⇒ ra_nfields td ti ⟨ kc_nz , ∅ ⟩ tnf ∈ lrel $ >
  $ G ⇒ ra_add tnp tnf tnq ∈ lrel $ >
  $ G ⇒ ra_add tii ⟨ kc_s , scons tfi ∅ ⟩ tnf ∈ lrel $ >
  $ G ⇒ ra_spine ⟨ kc_app , scons tY (scons tf ∅) ⟩ tmj tii ∈ lrel $ >
  $ G ⇒ ra_proj_ok tg td ti tfi ∈ lrel3 J $ >
  $ G ⇒ ra_ctor_ty td ti ⟨ kc_nz , ∅ ⟩ tCT ∈ lrel $ >
  $ G ⇒ ra_sty tg ⟨ kc_ind_ctor , scons td (scons ti (scons ⟨ kc_nz , ∅ ⟩ ∅)) ⟩ tCT tmj tT2 ∈ lrel3 J $ >
  $ G ⇒ tmj ∊ ofsort lsig lopen ks_expr $ >
  $ G ⇒ ti ∊ ofsort lsig lopen ks_nat $ >
  $ G ⇒ tb2 ∊ trees ω $ >
  $ G ⇒ dt u (mcv H) ⟨ kc_proj , scons tb2 (scons tfi (scons tmj ∅)) ⟩ w r = dt u (mcv H) tf w r $;




